    "## Assignment: DataFrame Operations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a Pandas DataFrame with 3 columns and 5 rows filled with random integers. Add a new column that is the product of the first two columns.\n2. Create a Pandas DataFrame with 3 columns and 4 rows filled with random integers. Compute the row-wise and column-wise sum."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# 1) 3 cols x 5 rows random; new column = product of first two columns\nnp.random.seed(1201)\ndf = pd.DataFrame(np.random.randint(1, 11, size=(5, 3)), columns=['X', 'Y', 'Z'])\ndf['Product'] = df['X'] * df['Y']\nprint(\"DataFrame with new 'Product' column:\"); print(df)\n\n# 2) 3 cols x 4 rows random; row-wise and column-wise sum\nnp.random.seed(1202)\ndf = pd.DataFrame(np.random.randint(1, 11, size=(4, 3)), columns=['A', 'B', 'C'])\nprint(\"DataFrame:\"); print(df)\nprint(\"Row-wise sum:\"); print(df.sum(axis=1))\nprint(\"Column-wise sum:\"); print(df.sum(axis=0))\n"
