    "## Assignment: Data Aggregation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a Pandas DataFrame with 2 columns: 'Category' and 'Value'. Fill the 'Category' column with random categories ('A', 'B', 'C') and the 'Value' column with random integers. Group the DataFrame by 'Category' and compute the sum and mean of 'Value' for each category.\n2. Create a Pandas DataFrame with 3 columns: 'Product', 'Category', and 'Sales'. Fill the DataFrame with random data. Group the DataFrame by 'Category' and compute the total sales for each category."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# 1) 2 cols Category + Value; group by Category; sum and mean\nnp.random.seed(1401)\ndf = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Category': np.random.choice(['A', 'B', 'C'], size=12),\n    'Value': np.random.randint(1, 21, size=12)\n})\nprint(\"DataFrame:\"); print(df)\nprint(\"Sum of Value by Category:\"); print(df.groupby('Category')['Value'].sum())\nprint(\"Mean of Value by Category:\"); print(df.groupby('Category')['Value'].mean())\n\n# 2) 3 cols Product, Category, Sales; group by Category; total sales\nnp.random.seed(1402)\ndf = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Product': ['P' + str(i) for i in range(1, 10)],\n    'Category': np.random.choice(['X', 'Y'], size=9),\n    'Sales': np.random.randint(100, 1001, size=9)\n})\nprint(\"DataFrame:\"); print(df)\nprint(\"Total sales by Category:\"); print(df.groupby('Category')['Sales'].sum())\n"
   ],
