    "## Assignment: Merging DataFrames"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create two Pandas DataFrames with a common column. Merge the DataFrames using the common column.\n2. Create two Pandas DataFrames with different columns. Concatenate the DataFrames along the rows and along the columns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# 1) Two DataFrames with a common column; merge on that column\nnp.random.seed(1501)\ndf1 = pd.DataFrame({'Key': ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D'],\n                    'Value1': np.random.randint(1, 10, size=4)})\ndf2 = pd.DataFrame({'Key': ['B', 'D', 'E', 'F'],\n                    'Value2': np.random.randint(100, 200, size=4)})\nprint(\"DataFrame 1:\"); print(df1)\nprint(\"DataFrame 2:\"); print(df2)\nmerged = pd.merge(df1, df2, on='Key', how='outer')\nprint(\"Merged (outer join on 'Key'):\"); print(merged)\n\n# 2) Two DataFrames with different columns; concat along rows and along columns\ndf_r1 = pd.DataFrame({'X': [1, 2, 3], 'Y': [4, 5, 6]})\ndf_r2 = pd.DataFrame({'X': [7, 8, 9], 'Y': [10, 11, 12]})\ndf_c1 = pd.DataFrame({'A': [1, 2], 'B': [3, 4]})\ndf_c2 = pd.DataFrame({'C': [5, 6], 'D': [7, 8]})\nprint(\"Concat along rows:\"); print(pd.concat([df_r1, df_r2], axis=0))\nprint(\"Concat along columns:\"); print(pd.concat([df_c1, df_c2], axis=1))\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
