    "## Assignment: Time Series Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a Pandas DataFrame with a datetime index and one column filled with random integers. Resample the DataFrame to compute the monthly mean of the values.\n2. Create a Pandas DataFrame with a datetime index ranging from '2021-01-01' to '2021-12-31' and one column filled with random integers. Compute the rolling mean with a window of 7 days."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# 1) datetime index + one random-int column; monthly mean\nnp.random.seed(1601)\ndates = pd.date_range('2021-01-01', periods=365, freq='D')\nts = pd.Series(np.random.randint(1, 100, size=365), index=dates)\nmonthly = ts.resample('ME').mean()\nprint(\"Original (first 5 values):\"); print(ts.head())\nprint(\"Monthly mean:\"); print(monthly)\n\n# 2) datetime index 2021-01-01..2021-12-31; one random-int column; 7-day rolling mean\nnp.random.seed(1602)\ndates = pd.date_range('2021-01-01', periods=365, freq='D')\ndf = pd.DataFrame({'Value': np.random.randint(1, 100, size=365)}, index=dates)\ndf['Rolling7'] = df['Value'].rolling(window=7).mean()\nprint(\"DataFrame with 7-day rolling mean (first 10 rows):\"); print(df.head(10))\n"
