    "## Assignment: MultiIndex DataFrame"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a Pandas DataFrame with a MultiIndex (hierarchical index). Perform some basic indexing and slicing operations on the MultiIndex DataFrame.\n2. Create a Pandas DataFrame with MultiIndex consisting of 'Category' and 'SubCategory'. Fill the DataFrame with random data and compute the sum of values for each 'Category' and 'SubCategory'."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# 1) MultiIndex DataFrame; basic indexing and slicing\narrays = [['A', 'A', 'A', 'B', 'B', 'B'], [1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3]]\nidx = pd.MultiIndex.from_arrays(arrays, names=['Letter', 'Num'])\ndf = pd.DataFrame({'Value': range(6)}, index=idx)\nprint(\"MultiIndex DataFrame:\"); print(df)\nprint(\"Subset at ('A', 1):\"); print(df.loc[('A', 1)])\nprint(\"Slice 'A' from 1 to 3:\"); print(df.loc['A'].loc[1:3])\n\n# 2) MultiIndex Category + SubCategory; sum of values for each category and subcategory\nnp.random.seed(1702)\narrays = [[f'C{i}' for i in range(8)], [f'S{i % 3}' for i in range(8)]]\nidx = pd.MultiIndex.from_arrays(arrays, names=['Category', 'SubCategory'])\ndf = pd.DataFrame({'Value': np.random.randint(1, 21, size=8)}, index=idx)\nprint(\"DataFrame:\"); print(df)\nprint(\"Sum of Values by Category and SubCategory:\"); print(\n    df.groupby(level=['Category', 'SubCategory'])['Value'].sum())\n"
   ],
